-- title:
--   Adelic Hecke eigenvalue of a lift at ℓ ∤ M
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 1$, let $\varepsilon$ be a Dirichlet character mod $M$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and let $h$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_1(M)$ satisfying [`CuspForm.HasNebentypus`](def/CuspForm_PrimitiveFormGamma1.html#L13) for $\varepsilon$, that is $h(\gamma\tau) = \varepsilon(\gamma_{11} \bmod M)\,(\gamma_{10}\tau+\gamma_{11})^{2}h(\tau)$ for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M)$ and every $\tau$ in the upper half-plane. Let $\Phi$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ which is an adelic lift of $h$ in the sense of [`CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOfGamma1`](def/CuspForm_AdelicLiftGamma1.html#L14): it is invariant under left multiplication by the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, invariant under right multiplication by the image under [`AdelicDock.finEmbed`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L145) of the level-one subgroup at the ideal generated by $M$, and for every adelic $g$ whose finite component is trivial and whose real component [`LanglandsTunnell.ratArchGL2`](def/LanglandsTunnell_DeltaLift.html#L16) $g$ has positive determinant, $\Phi(g) = (h \mid_2 \mathrm{ratArchGL2}\,g)(i)$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid M$, and let $\rho_0,\dots,\rho_\ell \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_\ell)$ have underlying matrices $\begin{pmatrix}1 & i\\ 0 & \ell\end{pmatrix}$ for $i < \ell$ and $\begin{pmatrix}\ell & 0\\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$ for $i = \ell$. Let $\lambda \in \mathbb{C}$ be such that the $q$-expansion coefficients of $h$ (coefficients of `qExpansion 1`) satisfy, for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, $a_{\ell n}(h) + \varepsilon(\ell)\,\ell^{2-1}\,[\ell \mid n]\,a_{n/\ell}(h) = \lambda\,a_n(h)$. Then for every $x$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$, $$\sum_{i=0}^{\ell} \Phi\bigl(x \cdot \mathrm{padicToAdelic}_\ell(\rho_i^{-1})\bigr) = \varepsilon(\ell)^{-1}\lambda\,\Phi(x),$$ where $\rho_i^{-1}$ is placed at the place $\ell$ and the identity elsewhere. The assertion is for all adelic $x$, not only those with trivial finite part.
--
--   This is the adelic–classical dictionary for the Hecke operator $T_\ell$ at a prime away from the level, in the direction "classical weight-two eigenform with nebentypus $\varepsilon$ gives an adelic eigenfunction", the factor $\varepsilon(\ell)^{-1}$ coming from the diamond operator $\langle \ell \rangle$ attached to the diagonal coset representative. It is used in the study of primitive forms, in particular in the bound on factorizations for elements of the fixed submodule at $K_1$ over $\mathbb{Q}_\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_HasNebentypus_sum_apply_padicToAdelic_eq_mul_of_isAdelicLiftOfGamma1_of_qCoeff_hecke_eq.lean

